  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "2002 OM2002-01 (28 July - 11 Aug 2002): US-Japan Cooperative Survey Data - R/V Oshoro Maru (Cruise ID: OM2002-01)",
  "description": "The Alaska Fisheries Science Center FOCI program conducted a summer survey in the eastern Bering Sea shelf region for walleye pollock larvae and juveniles. Data collected include pollock, seawater temperature, seawater salinity, chlorophyll, nutrients, and microzooplankton. Cruise ID: MF2002-07 (28 July - 11 August 2002) Survey vessels: R/V Oshoro Maru For preliminary survey results see http://www.pmel.noaa.gov/foci/operations/instructions/2002/OM02/1om02CruiseReport.htm\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To continue the long-term acquisition of biological and physical data relating to the summer abundance of walleye pollock (Theragra chalcogramma) larvae and juveniles in the eastern Bering sea shelf region. This is a continuing cooperative research effort between FOCI and the scientists at Hokkaido University of Hakodate, Japan.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23569824",
